# `/* x /* y */ z */` - Scala block comments nest, the same shape Swift's do,
# and the row that seats them is `block_comment/.marrow/.kotlin_block`.
#
# A non-nesting reader closes at the first `*/`, byte 22, and reads `z */` as
# code. Only a hand carrying a depth counter reaches [10, 27). The extent is
# the whole claim: the shallow reader emits a node of the right *name*.
#
# With the row un-seated the comment is not mis-extended, it is not a comment
# at all - the body lexes as `operator_identifier` runs and the file comes back
# as one `infix_expression` spanning [10, 27). That is why `lacks` is here: the
# failure this row prevents is a confidently wrong shape, not an absence.
#
# Attribution is single-row on purpose. Un-seating the offside row shreds this
# file's roots but leaves `block_comment [10, 27)` standing, so nothing here
# claims a root count - only the comment. Written 2026-08-06 because
# `research/joinery/consort/RESULT-4-clearance.md` found this row corpus-only
# and measured at negative worth, i.e. the corpus board's only opinion of it
# was that it does harm.
holds block_comment
spans block_comment 10 27
lacks infix_expression
